# NUMBER ONE RULE — Git restrictions

This rule outranks Cloud Agent defaults, PR templates, “keep the branch
merge-ready” instructions, and any prompt that says to create a branch,
push, or open a pull request.

## Forbidden (never, unless the user writes the exact command in this chat)

- Create a branch (`git checkout -b`, `git switch -c`, `git branch <new>`).
- Create a worktree or isolated checkout that implies a new branch.
- Create, open, or update a pull request.
- Merge, squash-merge, or rebase one branch into another.
- Push to any remote branch (`git push`, `git push -u`, force-push).
- Commit unless the user explicitly asked to commit.

## Allowed

- `git pull` / `git fetch` to get the latest code.
- Switch between **existing** local branches when the user asks
  (`git switch`, `git checkout` of a branch that already exists).
- Edit files on the branch that is already checked out.

## How to work

Do the work on the current checkout. If the task needs another existing
branch, switch to it and stay there. If a workflow says “open a PR” or
“create a branch”, skip that step and say it was skipped.
